\section{Case Studies: Tensor Compilation, Quantum Computing}\label{sec:case-studies}

\subsection{Tensor Compilation (MLIR + IREE)}\label{sec:tensor-compilation}

The IREE (Intermediate Representation Execution Environment) project uses MLIR to compile tensor programs for diverse hardware:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Input:} TensorFlow/JAX/PyTorch model (as MHLO dialect).
  \item \textbf{High-level optimization:} Fusion, constant folding, layout optimization (MHLO $\to$ Linalg).
  \item \textbf{Loop transformation:} Tiling, parallelization, vectorization (Linalg $\to$ Affine/SCF).
  \item \textbf{Hardware-specific lowering:} Generate code for CPU (LLVM), GPU (SPIR-V/CUDA), or TPU.
\end{enumerate}

The multi-level approach enables:
\begin{itemize}
  \item High-level optimizations (fusion) that are impossible at the loop level.
  \item Hardware-specific optimizations (GPU tiling, vectorization) at the appropriate level.
  \item A single compiler that targets multiple hardware platforms.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Quantum Computing (QIRO, QuiRL)}\label{sec:quantum-compilation}

Quantum computing compilers use multi-level IRs to optimize quantum circuits:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Quantum dialect.} High-level quantum operations (gates, measurements, error correction).
  \item \textbf{Circuit dialect.} Quantum circuits as sequences of gates.
  \item \textbf{Pulse dialect.} Low-level pulse sequences for specific hardware.
\end{enumerate}

Optimizations at the quantum level include:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Gate cancellation.} Adjacent inverse gates cancel: $H \cdot H = I$.
  \item \textbf{Circuit rewriting.} Replace expensive gate sequences with equivalent cheaper ones.
  \item \textbf{Qubit routing.} Map logical qubits to physical qubits, minimizing SWAP gates.
\end{itemize}

\begin{verbatim}
  // Quantum dialect:
  %q0 = quantum.alloc : !quantum.qubit
  %q1 = quantum.alloc : !quantum.qubit
  quantum.h %q0                  // Hadamard on q0
  quantum.cnot %q0, %q1          // CNOT: q0 control, q1 target
  quantum.h %q0                  // Hadamard on q0
  // Optimization: H-CNOT-H = a specific gate sequence
\end{verbatim}

