\subsection{Multi-Level IR for Other Domains}\label{sec:multi-level-other}

The multi-level IR approach extends beyond machine learning:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Circuit design.} High-level hardware descriptions lowered to gate-level netlists and then to physical layout.
  \item \textbf{Database queries.} Relational algebra lowered to query plans and then to execution operators.
  \item \textbf{Graphics shaders.} High-level shading languages lowered through optimization passes to GPU machine code.
  \item \textbf{Scientific computing.} PDE specifications lowered to discretized forms and then to parallel loop nests.
\end{itemize}

\begin{verbatim}
  // Multi-level IR for database queries:
  // Level 1: Relational algebra
  result = project(name, filter(age > 18, users))

  // Level 2: Query plan
  Scan(users) -> Filter(age > 18) -> Project(name)

  // Level 3: Execution operators
  for row in scan(users):
    if row.age > 18:
      emit(row.name)

  // Level 4: Machine code
  // Loop with comparison, branch, and memory access
\end{verbatim}

